      "writtenOn": "2026-01-30T13:58:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion. I’ve addressed this by switching away from the legacy attr/xattr.h and using the glibc xattr API from \u003csys/xattr.h\u003e with fgetxattr(), so there’s no additional dependency on libattr1.\n\nI considered vfs_getextattr_value(), but its signature requires a struct vfs_fsal_obj_handle *. In this path we only have a generic struct fsal_obj_handle * and we want to keep the function fsal_common_is_referral() with minimal changes. Using the standard \u003csys/xattr.h\u003e API keeps the change small and portable within Linux/glibc.",
      "parentUuid": "6a959a75_378ac294",
